**I agree with the targeted replay.** Both clean runs found the $720–745B estimate. The replay should show whether c8 files it under the old four-company 2026 question while preserving that it measures total spending.

**Test.** Use the 11 frozen September 7–20 articles for M04 and M17, plus article 223 as a five-company and 2027 control. Replay those 12 articles against each of old-2 and old-3’s day-start question lists. Keep the old answer choices and September 6 history. Build one frozen-judge request per question and run using the newly filed evidence. Have both card readers assess the four answers blind beside the archived old answers. [Frozen matters](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json)

**Pass lines.** All four judge requests contain the decisive, source-verified passages filed by c8. Zero five-company, 2027, or total-spending figures are presented as direct answers to four-company 2026 data-center spending. Anthropic talks stay unconfirmed. Zero standalone NVIDIA financial questions are proposed, including on article 181, which contains NVIDIA revenue. Both readers support all four answers.

**Attainable result.** The passages exist in both clean runs, so 4/4 deliveries and up to 4/4 supported answers are possible. The stored-results ceilings remain **6** under D382/D505 and **10** with Alex’s exception. Archived token usage prices 24 c8 calls and four judge calls at **$0.33–$0.42** before retries. This review cost $0. [Stored runs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run)

The test can show whether the changed filing works on these two matters. Automatic opening, repeat grouping, full-window performance, and release readiness remain untested.

CONSENSUS: Replay 12 articles against two stored question lists and blind-read four answers, subject to Alex’s approval.
